<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <POU Name="FB_GetPLCHostname" Id="{bd570dd7-dba7-4a18-a0ee-a97d90c7deaf}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
    FB_GetPLCHostname - reads this PLC's own hostname over ADS.

    PURPOSE
        Reports the hostname (computer name) of the target the program runs
        on, so callers that must identify this PLC in a text record - for
        example the "Logging system online" JSON document FB_LogHandler emits
        - do not each have to build their own ADS request.

    USAGE
        Call every cycle with bEnable := TRUE and use sHostname once bDone is
        TRUE:

            fbGetHostName : FB_GetPLCHostname;
            fbGetHostName(bEnable := TRUE, sHostname => GVL_Logger.sPlcHostname);

        There is no execute edge: bEnable level-enables the block, bDone
        latches the successful result, bError reports the failing one.

    OBJECTIVES
        - Wrap Tc2_Utilities.FB_GetHostName - which needs a NetID, an execute
          edge and a busy/error handshake - in a level-enabled block with a
          latched bDone, so a caller only supplies TRUE and reads a string.
        - Address the local system only: sNetID is fixed to '' (empty AMS
          NetID = the PLC this code runs on), so the block cannot be pointed
          at a remote target by accident.
        - Re-arm the child block once before the first request, so a bExecute
          that is already TRUE cannot swallow the first command.
        - Stop polling once the hostname is known: bDone gates the request, so
          a settled PLC issues no further ADS traffic.

    HISTORY
        2021-10-22 / Ken Lauer
            Block created; split out of the combined IP-address helper, with
            the periodic retry added in the same change.
        2021-11-30 / Ken Lauer
            Enable input renamed from bExecute to bEnable.
        2026-11-27 / Scirix Agent
            Added this header comment and the member comments below;
            documentation only, no behaviour change (convention
            conv_321640e095c0).

    NOTE
        Behaviour read off the implementation below, recorded so the next
        maintainer does not have to re-derive it:
        - bDone latches TRUE and is never cleared inside the block; only a PLC
          restart or a re-download resets it.
        - The retry path does not currently fire. bReset is a single-scan
          pulse, so tRetry (a TON driven by bReset) never accumulates
          tRetryDelay and tRetry.Q is never TRUE. The block therefore makes one
          acquisition attempt per PLC start; if that attempt fails, bExecute
          stays TRUE, which is not a re-trigger edge for the ADS block.
          tRetryDelay documents intended behaviour, not achieved behaviour.
*)
FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_GetPLCHostname
VAR_INPUT
    // TRUE enables hostname acquisition. While it is FALSE the body is
    // skipped: the child block is not called and every output keeps its
    // last value.
    bEnable			: BOOL;
    // Retry interval, TIME (ms resolution). Intended as the delay before a
    // failed acquisition is attempted again; default T#10s. Not currently
    // reached - see the NOTE in the POU header.
    tRetryDelay		: TIME := T#10s;
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
    // Hostname (computer name) of this PLC as returned by FB_GetHostName.
    // T_MaxString = STRING(255); no units. Written once, when the request
    // completes without error, and left untouched otherwise (so it stays
    // '' until the first successful acquisition).
    sHostname		: T_MaxString;
    // Latched completion flag: TRUE once sHostname has been captured and
    // the request is finished. Never cleared inside the block, so it stays
    // TRUE until the PLC restarts or is re-downloaded. Callers use it as
    // "the hostname is available" and as the gate that stops polling.
    bDone 			: BOOL;
    // Acquisition failed. Mirrors fbGetHostName.bError, so it is not latched
    // here: it follows the child block, which clears it only when re-armed
    // with bExecute = FALSE. bDone remains FALSE while bError is TRUE.
    bError			: BOOL;
END_VAR
VAR
    // Tc2_Utilities hostname reader. sNetID is fixed to '' (local system)
    // by the body, and bExecute is driven by this block, not by the caller.
    fbGetHostName	: FB_GetHostName;

    // Retry timer, TIME: measures tRetryDelay after the re-arm pulse. As
    // written its IN is a single-scan pulse, so Q is never reached (see the
    // NOTE in the POU header).
    tRetry 			: TON;
    // One-scan re-arm pulse: drives fbGetHostName.bExecute FALSE for one scan
    // (the falling edge re-arms the ADS block) and starts tRetry. Cleared
    // again in the same cycle, after the child call and the timer.
    bReset			: BOOL;
    // TRUE from the first enabled scan onwards, so the re-arm happens once
    // per PLC start instead of every cycle. FALSE again after a download or
    // a restart.
    bInitialized	: BOOL := FALSE;

END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[IF bEnable THEN
    fbGetHostName.sNetID := '';

    IF NOT bInitialized OR (tRetry.Q AND NOT bDone) THEN
        bReset			:= TRUE;
        bInitialized	:= TRUE;
        fbGetHostName(bExecute:=FALSE);
    END_IF

    tRetry(IN:=bReset, PT:=tRetryDelay);

    bReset := FALSE;

    IF NOT bDone THEN
        fbGetHostName(bExecute:=TRUE, bError=>bError);
        IF NOT (fbGetHostName.bBusy OR bError) THEN
            sHostname	:= fbGetHostName.sHostName;
            bDone 		:= TRUE;
        END_IF
    END_IF
END_IF]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>